body=intro('YOUR INFORMATION','Privacy Policy','How Morocco Explorer Tours collects, uses and protects information shared through this website and during trip planning.')+f'''<section class="container prose collection legal-page"><p>Morocco Explorer Tours respects your privacy and is committed to protecting the personal information you share with us when you browse this website, contact us, request a private Morocco tour or continue with a booking.</p><h2>1. Why we collect personal information</h2><p>We collect personal information so we can answer enquiries, prepare travel proposals, arrange private tours, manage bookings, provide customer support and meet legal or operational requirements related to travel services.</p><p>Depending on the service requested, Morocco Explorer Tours may act as the data controller for retail travel services, enquiries and marketing communications.</p><h2>2. Personal information we may collect</h2><p>The information we collect depends on how you interact with us. It may include your name, email address, phone number, travel dates, arrival and departure details, group size, accommodation preferences, tour interests and any notes you choose to share.</p><p>When needed to arrange a confirmed trip, we may ask for passport or travel-document details, dietary requirements, medical or accessibility information, emergency contact details and payment-related information. Sensitive information is requested only when relevant to your travel arrangements and with your consent.</p><h2>3. How we collect information</h2><p>We collect information directly from you when you contact us by email, WhatsApp, phone, social media or an online form; when you request a quote; when you confirm a tour; or when someone travelling with you provides details on your behalf.</p><p>The trip planner on this website prepares a brief in your browser. It does not automatically submit the form to a server or store your answers in browser storage. If you choose to copy, download, email or send the brief by WhatsApp, the selected service handles that information under its own privacy terms.</p><h2>4. How we use your information</h2><p>We use personal information to respond to enquiries, design itineraries, confirm availability, process bookings, coordinate hotels, transport, guides and activities, provide travel updates, improve our services and comply with applicable laws.</p><p>We may also use your contact details to follow up on a requested proposal or booking. We only send marketing messages where permitted by law or where you have chosen to receive them.</p><h2>5. Sharing information with suppliers</h2><p>We do not sell, rent or trade personal information. We share only the information needed to provide your travel services with trusted suppliers such as accommodation providers, transport operators, local guides, activity providers, payment processors and technology providers.</p><p>Suppliers receive only the details required for their part of the service, including relevant dietary, medical or accessibility information when necessary for your safety and comfort.</p><h2>6. International transfers</h2><p>Travel planning may require information to be shared with suppliers or service providers outside your home country. We take reasonable steps to ensure that personal information is handled appropriately and only for the purpose of arranging or supporting your requested travel services.</p><h2>7. Cookies and website data</h2><p>This website uses local files such as images, styles and scripts to provide the browsing experience. The current version does not include advertising trackers, third-party fonts or analytics scripts. Standard hosting logs may process technical information such as IP address, browser type, requested page and request time to deliver and secure the site.</p><h2>8. Your rights</h2><p>Subject to applicable law, you may ask to access, correct, update, restrict or delete personal information we hold about you. You may also object to certain processing or request a copy of your information in a portable format.</p><p>To make a privacy request, contact us using the details below. We may need to verify your identity before responding.</p><h2>9. Security and retention</h2><p>We use reasonable physical, electronic and procedural safeguards to protect personal information against loss, misuse, unauthorised access, alteration or disclosure.</p><p>We keep personal information only for as long as needed for the purpose collected, including booking administration, legal, accounting, dispute-resolution and service-improvement requirements.</p><h2>10. Third-party links and services</h2><p>Our website may link to third-party services such as WhatsApp, email apps, social media platforms or review and booking platforms. Their privacy practices are governed by their own policies, and you should review those policies before sharing information with them.</p><h2>11. Updates to this policy</h2><p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any updated version will be posted on this page with a revised date. Continuing to use the website or our services after changes are posted means you accept the updated policy.</p>{legal_contact()}</section>'''
write(current,'Privacy Policy','Read how Morocco Explorer Tours collects, uses and protects information shared through this website and during private Morocco trip planning.',body)
current='terms-and-conditions.html'
body=intro('BOOKING TERMS','Terms and Conditions','The booking terms for private Morocco tours arranged with Morocco Explorer Tours.')+f'''<section class="container prose collection legal-page"><p>These Terms and Conditions apply when you enquire about, book or travel on a private tour arranged by Morocco Explorer Tours. By confirming a booking, you accept these terms for yourself and for every participant included in your reservation.</p><h2>1. Booking confirmation and payment</h2><p>After your itinerary, travel dates, inclusions and final price are agreed, Morocco Explorer Tours will provide payment instructions. Unless different written terms are agreed for your booking, your reservation is confirmed when we receive a deposit of 20% to 30% of the total invoice amount.</p><p>The remaining balance is due according to the written proposal or invoice. For some tours, the balance may be payable in cash on the day of the tour. Your written proposal or invoice should be checked carefully before payment.</p><h2>2. Booking changes and cancellations</h2><p>If you need to change your booking, contact us as soon as possible. We will try to help, but changes depend on supplier availability, transport schedules and any costs already committed.</p><p>If you cancel your trip, cancellation fees are calculated from the date we receive written notice from you:</p><ul><li>30 days or more before the tour start date: the deposit is retained.</li><li>Less than 30 days before the tour start date: no refund is available and full payment may be required.</li></ul><p>Different cancellation terms may apply if they are clearly stated in your written proposal, invoice or supplier conditions.</p><h2>3. Events outside our control</h2><p>We cannot accept liability for loss, damage, delay, additional expense or refund requests caused by events outside our reasonable control. These may include war or threat of war, civil unrest, airport closures, industrial action, terrorism or threat of terrorism, natural disasters, severe weather, road closures, public-health restrictions, government advice or any other circumstances that make travel unsafe or impracticable.</p><h2>4. Special requirements</h2><p>Please tell us before confirming your booking about dietary restrictions, medical needs, mobility needs, allergies or other requirements that may affect your trip. We will share relevant information with suppliers where needed to support your comfort and safety.</p><p>Requests such as preferred room type, hotel location or bed configuration should be made at the time of booking. We will try to arrange them, but they cannot be guaranteed unless confirmed in writing.</p><h2>5. Transportation</h2><p>Vehicles used for Morocco Explorer Tours services are arranged with licensed local transport providers appropriate for the number of passengers and the route. Seat availability, luggage space and vehicle type should be confirmed in your written proposal.</p><h2>6. Travel insurance</h2><p>All travellers are responsible for having suitable travel insurance. Your policy should cover personal belongings, money and passports, personal accident or injury, medical expenses, emergency medical treatment, repatriation and cancellation.</p><p>If your itinerary includes activities such as camel riding, horse riding, trekking, cycling, quad biking, mountain routes or travel above 2,000 metres, make sure your insurance covers those activities.</p><h2>7. Liability and local suppliers</h2><p>Morocco Explorer Tours arranges private travel services using local suppliers such as transport providers, accommodation providers, guides and activity operators. We are not responsible for injury, illness, death, loss, delay or damage caused by the acts, omissions or conditions of third-party suppliers where we have acted with reasonable care in arranging the service.</p><p>Safety standards, facilities and operating practices in Morocco may differ from those in your home country. Travellers are responsible for following local guidance, supplier instructions and reasonable safety advice.</p><h2>8. Itinerary changes</h2><p>Itineraries may change because of weather, road conditions, mechanical issues, supplier availability, driver or guide health, local events or other conditions beyond our control. Morocco Explorer Tours may adjust the route, timing or order of activities where needed for safety, comfort or practicality.</p><p>We recommend scheduling onward travel no earlier than the day after the end of a long private tour, as delays can occur on Moroccan roads and in remote areas.</p><h2>9. Travel documents</h2><p>You are responsible for checking passport, visa, entry, health and onward-ticket requirements for Morocco before travel. Morocco Explorer Tours is not liable for missed services, denied entry, repatriation costs or additional expenses caused by incomplete or invalid travel documents.</p><h2>10. Activity equipment and safety</h2><p>For activities such as cycling, trekking, horse riding, camel riding or quad biking, equipment availability and standards may vary by supplier and location. Bring your own specialist safety equipment where required by your insurance, comfort level or home-country standards.</p><h2>11. Privacy and use of information</h2><p>Personal information provided during enquiry or booking is used to arrange travel services and communicate with you about your trip. Relevant details may be shared with hotels, transport providers, guides and activity suppliers. Read our {a('privacy.html','Privacy Policy')} for more information.</p><p>We may request permission to use photographs, feedback or case studies from your tour on our website or social media. If you do not want to be featured, tell us before or during your trip.</p><h2>12. Complaints</h2><p>If something goes wrong during your tour, tell your driver, guide, accommodation provider or Morocco Explorer Tours as soon as possible so we have a chance to resolve the issue while you are still travelling.</p><p>If the issue cannot be resolved locally, contact us with full details. We will review the matter and respond as fairly as possible based on the services booked, supplier information and circumstances.</p>{legal_contact()}</section>'''
write(current,'Terms and Conditions','Read the booking terms for private Morocco tours arranged with Morocco Explorer Tours, including deposits, cancellations, insurance and itinerary changes.',body)
